      <item>
         <title><![CDATA[Ford says he 'can't wait' for U.S. midterms]]></title>
         <link>https://www.cbc.ca/player/play/9.7396074?cmp=rss</link>
         <description><![CDATA[<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/6f72ad21-7740-40b1-b449-3dfa215cbe40,1793027363738/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%28220%2C91%2C1472%2C828%29%3B' alt='Ontario Premier Doug Ford, Ottawa. Oct. 26. 2026.' width='620' height='349' title='Ontario Premier Doug Ford, Ottawa. Oct. 26. 2026.'/><p>Asked whether increased talk of a possible Canada-U.S. trade deal may be related to the upcoming U.S. midterm elections, Ontario Premier Doug Ford said he believes it's a 'combination' of things. 'They're going for election down there and I don't think President Trump's doing too well. And I think the trade deal with Canada is affecting them,' said Ford.</p>]]></description>
